{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_016RyzhJTJYspjpcVtSWxUSh","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Project State Summary\n\n**Problem**: GNU coreutils have no formal specs accessible to implementers. This project derives formal specifications from C source, generates Go implementations via AI agents, and verifies parity through differential testing against Homebrew GNU reference binaries.\n\n**Architecture**: A four-stage pipeline (extract → specify → synthesize → verify) with `cmd/` per-utility packages, shared `pkg/` libraries (testutils, sys, format, hashutil, sizeparse, encutil), and `docs/specs/` holding SRDs and use cases. Code generation is driven by mage-claude-orchestrator; specs are human-authored.\n\n**Current state**: Most foundational infrastructure (rel00.0) is implemented. Many utilities through rel03.1 are implemented. The latest commits just completed `cmd/nl` R1.1-R2.4 (tasks 5257-5258). Numerous utilities from rel05.0 onward remain unstarted.\n\n**Current release**: rel05.0 (text stream transforms: echo, tac, nl, fold). nl has R3.1-R3.4 and R4.1-R4.4 remaining. fold has R1.1-R4.4 all ready. echo and tac have no requirements in ready state.\n\n## Priority Reasoning\n\nThe earliest incomplete release with ready requirements is **rel05.0**. Within it:\n- **nl** (srd022-nl): R1-R2 just completed. R3.1-R3.4 and R4.1-R4.4 are ready — finish this utility first.\n- **fold** (srd023-fold): All 15 requirements ready — start this utility.\n\nnl and fold are independent packages (no cross-dependency). Canonical ordering: cmd/fold < cmd/nl alphabetically.\n\n## Weight Budget Verification\n\n```\nTask 0: srd023-fold R1.1(w=1) + R1.2(w=1) + R1.3(w=1) + R1.4(w=1) = 4 ≤ 4 ✓\nTask 1: srd023-fold R2.1(w=1) + R2.2(w=1) + R2.3(w=1) = 3 ≤ 4 ✓\nTask 2: srd022-nl R3.1(w=1) + R3.2(w=1) + R3.3(w=1) + R3.4(w=1) = 4 ≤ 4 ✓\nTask 3: srd022-nl R4.1(w=1) + R4.2(w=1) + R4.3(w=1) + R4.4(w=1) = 4 ≤ 4 ✓\n```\n\n```yaml\n- index: 0\n  title: \"[stitch] cmd/fold: implement srd023-fold R1.1-R1.4\"\n  dependency: -1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/specs/software-requirements/srd023-fold.yaml (SRD for fold utility -- read all requirements, focus on R1.1-R1.4)\n      - pkg/testutils/difftest.go (DiffTest struct and RunDiffTests for differential testing)\n      - pkg/sys/sigpipe.go (InstallSIGPIPEHandler for SIGPIPE handling)\n\n    files:\n      - path: cmd/fold/main.go\n        action: create\n        note: fold utility main implementation covering srd023-fold R1.1-R1.4\n      - path: cmd/fold/fold_test.go\n        action: create\n        note: differential tests for srd023-fold R1.1-R1.4\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: Implement srd023-fold requirement R1.1\n      - id: R2\n        text: Implement srd023-fold requirement R1.2\n      - id: R3\n        text: Implement srd023-fold requirement R1.3\n      - id: R4\n        text: Implement srd023-fold requirement R1.4\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: Call sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler() at the start of main to match GNU coreutils behavior when piped\n      - id: D2\n        text: Use testutils.BuildBinary(t, \".\") and testutils.RunDiffTests for differential testing against the gfold reference binary\n      - id: D3\n        text: Call exec.LookPath(\"gfold\") and t.Skip if the reference binary is not found\n      - id: D4\n        text: Set LC_ALL=C in test Env to ensure consistent output comparison\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: cmd/fold/main.go compiles without errors -- go build -o bin/fold ./cmd/fold/\n      - id: AC2\n        text: All differential tests pass -- go test ./cmd/fold/ -count=1\n      - id: AC3\n        text: go vet ./cmd/fold/ reports no issues\n      - id: AC4\n        text: SRD requirements R1.1 through R1.4 are implemented with corresponding test cases\n\n- index: 1\n  title: \"[stitch] cmd/fold